winex11: Keep a plain owned popup unmanaged when it is only activated.

"Activated windows are managed": when an application activates a window with SetActiveWindow, the SetWindowPos
that comes with it has no SWP_NOACTIVATE, so an owned popup that was shown unmanaged (SW_SHOWNA) was remapped as a
managed window. The window manager then focused it and the focus went back and forth between it and its owner.
InDesign shows an invisible popup over a text selection that way and activates it; the remap made it drop the popup
in the middle of a shortcut, so after a double-click or a drag selection Ctrl was lost: Ctrl+Shift+B typed "B" over
the word and Ctrl+A typed "a" (2026-10-23, +win,+event traces). A plain popup (no caption, thick frame or system
menu, with an owner, not an app window) that is already shown unmanaged now stays unmanaged when it is only
activated. Its keyboard input still arrives, through the thread's focus window.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -3292,6 +3292,15 @@
     if ((is_managed = is_window_managed( hwnd, swp_flags, fullscreen ))) make_owner_managed( hwnd );
 
     if (!(data = get_win_data( hwnd ))) return;
+    /* A plain owned popup (no caption, frame or system menu) that is already shown unmanaged stays unmanaged when
+     * it is only activated (SetActiveWindow): remapping it as a managed window lets the window manager focus it and
+     * move the focus back and forth. InDesign shows an invisible popup over a text selection with SW_SHOWNA and then
+     * activates it; the remap made it drop the popup in the middle of a shortcut, and Ctrl was lost (Ctrl+A typed
+     * "a"). The keyboard still reaches the popup: input goes to the thread's focus window. */
+    if (is_managed && !data->managed && data->desired_state.wm_state != WithdrawnState && !(swp_flags & SWP_SHOWWINDOW) &&
+        (new_style & WS_POPUP) && (new_style & WS_CAPTION) != WS_CAPTION && !(new_style & (WS_THICKFRAME | WS_SYSMENU)) &&
+        !(ex_style & WS_EX_APPWINDOW) && NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_OWNER ) && !fullscreen)
+        is_managed = FALSE;
     if (is_managed) window_set_managed( data, TRUE );
 
     old_rects = data->rects;
